From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:00:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] chore(llama-cpp): llama.cpp at upstream master 8e23278c,
 every patch carried onto it

LLAMA_VERSION moves from 78e0529 (2026-11-18) to master's 8e23278c
(2026-11-27), 299 commits later. Of the 24 patches in patches/, nine are
carried onto it (0008, 0012, 0013, 0015, 0016, 0017, 0022, 0023, 0026) and
the other fifteen apply as they are; the whole set applies with patch -p1
and no fuzz.

- 0012 (OmniVoice): the backbone's attention, feed-forward and output
  without the per-tensor scale arguments, which upstream folded into the
  tensors (#28898); its projector, gen-audio type and capability beside the
  speech models upstream added meanwhile (Moshi, VoxCPM2).
- 0026 (a BERT text pair): its own pooler hunk is gone, upstream keeps the
  pooler since #33122 (15fcfc7, BertForSequenceClassification); the GELU key
  is written for that class too, or MedCPT's cross-encoder would fall back
  to the tanh GELU.
- the others: context only (upstream's new lines next to ours).

grpc-server.cpp and prepare.sh take LocalAI's own fix for the decision
API's audio flag (#32578, LocalAI a1937e98): parse_questions(body, audio),
probed by prepare.sh so an older tree keeps the one-argument call.

Checked, on a CPU: every standalone test of the patches; the gRPC server
built and driven over gRPC - MedCPT's article encoder (67 pairs) and
cross-encoder (40 reranks) the same bytes as with 78e0529, two OmniVoice
clips (seed 1234) the same bytes, an invalid voice design refused with the
same reason; the server's parking and context-on-demand tests, 25 of 25.
The SYCL backend and libllama compile with icpx. Not run on a card.

